 is special  about it well imagine that in order to  promote the pawn white King has to move  somewhere and then only way to draw the  game for black is to provide series of  Queen Jack and in many instant what will  block the check with his queen and this  is the vital point of this position as  the black King is far away the chances  of getting counter check are completely  suppressed compared to the king anywhere  on the board let me demonstrate this  with two scenario where black king is in  and out of the drawing zone so the first  scenario I am going to take case black  is managed to get into the drawing zone  and get a comfortable draw so here  accurate responses came to b3 and now I  can choose either of this moves it  doesn't matter because black King is  right on the time to enter into the  drawing zone a sample line can goes like  this quint web 7 check King to be 2  entering into the drawing zone and now  in order to promote that pawn white king  has to come out so let's say King to g7  and there are many ways you can check  the king I am just giving you a simple  line Queen to g4 check Queen to g6 Queen  to d7 check King 2 at 6 so the only way  for white to win this game is to somehow  take his king to the far end and then  block the Queen check with his own queen  and let's see how black encounter all  this so Queen to d2 check cringy phi  quinn d6 check king at phi quindi even  check quincy for queen h1 check and now  this is the problem case as white has  also need to taken care of the H born so  now King has to go back that is king to  g6 and in fact no matter how many done  step white king can take he can never  reach to the far end you can deliver  infinite number of check from this  position and the beauty you can already  see due to the superior drawing zone  position of the black King white cannot  deliver any counter check the second  move I can try over here is King to g8  but I think this is most easy one as you  can deliver this check and after Queen  to f8 you can give another check and  after King to h8 only thing you have to  be careful here that you cannot  immediately enter into the drawing zone  but you have an easy way and that is  king to c2 and now black is completely  fine in the next move he's going to  enter into the drawing zone and create  an easy trough probably this concept is  easy to understood by going through the  original game as in the game black  certainly doesn't have the clue of  drawing zone and he continues with King  to d3 which is a big time mistake as you  are going away from the trans own  it is very instructive to see how  calcine managed to win this game he  continues with Queen to d7 checking the  king and still black king should help  going towards the drying zone instead of  that he prefer King to e 2 which is  outright a big blunder and from here  onwards there is no escape white plays  came to g8 so creating a space for  another Queen and now black is forced to  give some checks so Queen to g6 happen  in the game white plays King to f8  quintet sex check Queen to g7 Queen to  f4 check Queen to f7 and now you can see  the drawback of poor miss placement of  this King black will allow to give all  these checks but the problem is White  Queen will come in between and it will  give a counter check to the black King  and that's why black has the only check  available in this position that is Quint  well 6 King to e7 Queen to h4 check King  to e8 Queen to f4 check and now the  winning move of the game wonderful King  to a fade which highlights how pathetic  this King position is as black would  like to give these checks but  unfortunately white queen will come in  between and black is going to lose the  game last desperate try by black Queen  to d4 trying to stop the queening but  this is now just an easy pie Carlsen  give this track and after king to f2 and  promoting the second Queen it is just an  easy technical performance required by  white only few moves has been 